US-081 is not complete. The Linux release gate now passes, but several acceptance items remain unrun.

**What changed this round**
- The first `linux-release` build failed. `tests/src/core_assert_tests.cpp` used `ENGINE_DEBUG_ASSERT` inside `CHECK_NOTHROW`, which does not compile when `NDEBUG` is set. The helper it called also left an unused variable, which `-Werror` rejects. I guarded the helper with `#ifndef NDEBUG` and made the release branch call the macro directly.
- After the fix, `cmake --build --preset linux-release` passed and `ctest --preset linux-release-unit` passed 30 of 30.
- `docs/acceptance.md` now records the Linux release result, and `.ralph-tui/progress.md` has a new entry for this pass.

**Still not run**
- `win-release` build on Windows.
- `linux-gcc`. The local GCC 9.4 cannot build Jolt.
- `linux-asan` and `linux-sanitize`.
- The GPU suites: DX12 and Vulkan on Windows, and Vulkan on native Linux. This machine has no native Linux Vulkan device, and the RTX 5080 is visible only under WSL.
- The editor suite and visual smoke tests on both operating systems.
- The clean-copy offline build and the clean-directory package smoke tests.
- The full acceptance benchmark.

The earlier Windows gates (`ValidateVendor`, `win-dev`, `win-debug`, `win-unit`) passed before this round. I did not re-run them after the test fix, so the Windows debug and unit results predate it. The Linux debug and unit results also predate it, though the release unit run covers the same test files.
